# HugeIcons Usage Guidelines

## Overview
Always use HugeIcons instead of standard Icons throughout the Medito project. HugeIcons provide better visual consistency and are the preferred icon set for the app.

## Key Principles
- **Never use standard Icons** (`Icons.*`) in new code
- **Always use HugeIcons** (`HugeIcons.*`) for all icon implementations
- **Maintain visual consistency** across the entire application

## Common HugeIcons Examples
- `HugeIcons.solidSharpRepeat` - For repeat functionality (inactive state)
- `HugeIcons.solidStandardRepeatOne01` - For repeat functionality (active state)
- `HugeIcons.strokeStandardGoBackward10Sec` - For skip backward 10 seconds
- `HugeIcons.strokeStandardGoForward10Sec` - For skip forward 10 seconds
- `HugeIcons.solidRoundedPlayCircle` - For play button
- `HugeIcons.solidRoundedPauseCircle` - For pause button

## Import Statement
```dart
import 'package:hugeicons/hugeicons.dart';
```

## Usage Pattern
```dart
Icon(
  HugeIcons.solidSharpRepeat,
  size: 40,
  color: Colors.white,
)
```

## Migration Notes
When updating existing code, replace all instances of `Icons.*` with appropriate `HugeIcons.*` equivalents to maintain consistency.
